author: ascend
title: v0.34.0 released — Studio v1 milestone cut + in-app New-file fix
summary: 'Follow-up session after the v1 push. Fixed the reviewer''s #1 gap that surfaced in real use: atelier studio could list/open existing .atelier files but had no way to CREATE one from inside the app (empty dir dead-ended at a fake --new CLI hint; populated dir had no New action). Added a + New button to the sidebar header and a + New document button to the empty state, both wired to a createNewFile() client function that prompts for a name, builds a minimal starter doc via newStarterDoc() (1080x1080 + one centered title text layer), validates it round-trips through parseAtelier, POSTs to the existing /api/file endpoint, and refreshes+loads. No server change needed (POST /api/file already wrote arbitrary safe paths). Verified for real, not just typecheck: booted the studio against a temp dir, fetched the Vite-transpiled client main.ts (createNewFile/newStarterDoc/+New all present, no transpile error), and confirmed serializeAtelier(newStarterDoc()) round-trips through the schema. Then cut the v0.34.0 release: bumped 5 touched packages (cli 0.34.0, types 0.31.0, schema 0.28.0, studio 0.27.0, mcp 0.26.0), wrote a comprehensive CHANGELOG [0.34.0] entry covering the whole Studio v1 surface, synced the stale README version (was 0.25.1). Full workspace build green (14/14), 649/649 tests, 23/23 typechecks. Pushing 14 commits to origin/main (no tag, no npm publish — user''s chosen scope).'
